ition ensures nowhere differentiability?","options":["$a = 0$","$b = 1$","$a = b$","$ab \\gt 1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5e9827a1dcc7d039d352ed3e","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_weierstrass_function_eaa2b515_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $a = \\frac{1}{3}$ and $b = 2$. what can be safely concluded from $0 \\lt a \\lt 1$?","options":["The function is nowhere differentiable because $ab \\gt 1$.","The function is continuous everywhere.","The function is a polynomial.","The function is not defined."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"881a254c1cbe2f871d31d007","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_weierstrass_function_eaa2b515_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"In the original-paper version described, which extra feature appears in the cosine term?","options":["$x^2$","$\\pi x$","$\\mathrm{e}^x$","$\\log x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5464e79bc8a82103cb9cb115","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_weierstrass_function_eaa2b515_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly separates the two conditions?","options":["$ab \\gt 1$ gives continuity everywhere, while $0 \\lt a \\lt 1$ gives nowhere differentiability.","$0 \\lt a \\lt 1$ gives continuity everywhere, while $ab \\gt 1$ gives differentiability everywhere.","$0 \\lt a \\lt 1$ gives continuity everywhere, while $ab \\gt 1$ gives nowhere differentiability.","$ab \\gt 1$ alone gives both continuity everywhere and nowhere differentiability."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1cbb30a3547f7116756493eb","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_weierstrass_function_eaa2b515_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which series is mentioned as an earlier Riemann function also called the Weierstrass function in some textbooks?","options":["$\\sum_{n